---
title: Tech radar
weight: 40
---

<% radar = data.tech_radar %>
<% base = radar['meta']['base_path'] %>

<div class="radar-hero">
  <h1><%= current_page.data.title %></h1>
  <p>See which technologies are recommended at the Department for Education, which are worth trying, and which to move away from.</p>
</div>

<div class="radar-draft">
  <p class="govuk-body"><strong><%= radar_h(radar['meta']['status']) %> (<%= radar_h(radar['meta']['updated']) %>).</strong>
  This radar is built from a stock report of the software used across the department. The rings are a proposal
  and are still being reviewed by the tech community. Do not treat them as final policy yet.</p>
</div>

<p class="govuk-body">
  The tech radar helps teams choose technology for new work. It is a picture of what is in use across DfE
  and what we recommend. It does not replace the guidance in
  <a class="govuk-link" href="/guides/default-technology-stack/">The DfE Technology Stack</a>. Use it alongside that guidance.
</p>

<script type="application/json" id="tech-radar-data"><%= radar_json %></script>

<div id="tech-radar">
  <p id="tech-radar-fallback" class="govuk-body">
    The interactive radar needs JavaScript. You can still
    <a class="govuk-link" href="#browse-by-area">browse every technology by area</a>.
  </p>
</div>

<h2 id="how-to-read-the-radar">How to read the radar</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">
  Each dot is a technology. The closer a dot is to the centre, the more strongly we recommend it.
  Select a dot, or a card in grid view, to see more detail.
</p>

<h3>Rings</h3>

<dl class="radar-defs">
  <% radar['rings'].each do |ring| %>
    <div class="radar-defs-row">
      <dt><span class="radar-badge radar-badge--<%= radar_h(ring['id']) %>"><%= radar_h(ring['name']) %></span></dt>
      <dd><%= radar_h(ring['description']) %></dd>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</dl>

<h3>Quadrants</h3>

<dl class="radar-defs">
  <% radar['quadrants'].each do |quadrant| %>
    <div class="radar-defs-row">
      <dt><%= radar_h(quadrant['name']) %></dt>
      <dd><%= radar_h(quadrant['description']) %></dd>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</dl>

<h2 id="browse-by-area">Browse by area</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">Each area has its own page that lists the technologies by ring, with guidance and links.</p>

<% radar['quadrants'].each do |quadrant| %>
  <h3><%= radar_h(quadrant['name']) %></h3>
  <ul class="radar-area-cards">
    <% radar['areas'].select { |area| area['quadrant'] == quadrant['id'] }.each do |area| %>
      <% count = radar['entries'].count { |entry| entry['area'] == area['id'] } %>
      <li>
        <h4 class="govuk-heading-s"><a class="govuk-link" href="<%= base %><%= radar_h(area['id']) %>/"><%= radar_h(area['name']) %></a></h4>
        <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-font-size-16"><%= radar_h(area['description']) %></p>
        <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-font-size-16"><strong><%= count %></strong> technologies</p>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
<% end %>

<h2 id="core-dfe-stack">The core DfE stack</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">
  These are the technologies most commonly used to build and run services across the department.
  If you are starting a new service, begin here.
</p>

<%= partial('partials/radar_table', locals: { entries: radar_entries(nil, true), caption: 'Core DfE technology stack', show_area: true }) %>

<h2 id="keeping-the-radar-up-to-date">Keeping the radar up to date</h2>

<p class="govuk-body">
  The radar is reviewed regularly by the tech community. Anyone can suggest a change:
</p>

<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
  <li><a class="govuk-link" href="<%= radar_h(radar['meta']['edit_url']) %>">edit the radar data on GitHub</a> and raise a pull request</li>
  <li><a class="govuk-link" href="<%= radar_h(radar['meta']['issues_url']) %>">raise an issue</a> to suggest a new technology or a change of ring</li>
  <li>ask in <%= radar_h(radar['meta']['slack']) %> on Slack</li>
</ul>

<p class="govuk-body">
  See <a class="govuk-link" href="/guides/adding-new-guidance/#updating-the-tech-radar">Updating the tech radar</a> for how the data file works.
</p>
